  "body": "from my journal:\r\n\r\n```\r\nMar 06 06:07:23 ip-10-4-4-153 python[5779]:   File \"/opt/venvs/matrix-synapse/lib/python3.5/site-packages/synapse/rest/client/v1/login.py\", line 272, in do_jwt_login\r\nMar 06 06:07:23 ip-10-4-4-153 python[5779]:     from jwt.exceptions import InvalidTokenError\r\nMar 06 06:07:23 ip-10-4-4-153 python[5779]: builtins.ImportError: No module named 'jwt.exceptions'\r\n```\r\n\r\nYes, I have pyjwt installed in my venv.\r\n\r\nMatrix recently switched to python 3.5 in a venv from python 2 without a venv. This is the first time seeing this errror. Not sure if pyjwt is somehow different in 3.5",
